==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|déifier|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|deificāre}}, from {{term|deus||god}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdeɪ.ɪ.faɪ/|/ˈdiː.ɪ.faɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈdiː.ə.faɪ/|/ˈdeɪ.ə.faɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-deify.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-deify-2.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|deif|ies}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To make a [[god]] of (something or someone).
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To treat as [[worthy]] of worship; to regard as a [[deity]].

====Synonyms====
* {{qualifier|to make a god of something}}: [[apotheosize]], [[exalt]], [[idealize]]

====Related terms====
* [[deific]]
* [[deification]]
* [[deified]]

